 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-3.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(1,-3,8)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(1,-3).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(1,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,-3) & =\\frac{{1}^{2}+1}{{1}^{2}(-3)^{2}}+(-3)\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}-3(1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{25}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9f77ab83ff0ba5aac801d22370afc5a675d44ad23b296279e6507db4f0f22b6" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{16}{9}"] "category" "m