swer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{25}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-64968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P$ with $y$-coordinate $0$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=\\sqrt{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy+\\frac{\\pi }{4})$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-64968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $y=0$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(1,0).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(1,0):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =\\sqrt{2}(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-64968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9f77ab83ff0ba5aac801d22370afc5a675d44ad23b296279e6507db4f0f22b6" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-64968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-64968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" 