9" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+2\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-\\pi "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi -1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132579" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1-\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,0,8)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+4y+x$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(-2,0,8)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,0)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(-2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,0)} & =(-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+4(0)+(-2) \\\\  & =-2-2 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(-2,0)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(-2,0)}(y-0) \\\\ z-8 & =-4(y-0) \\\\ z & =-4y+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,0,8)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4y+8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9f77ab83ff0ba5aac801d22370afc5a675d44ad23b296279e6507db4f0f22b6" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4x\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=-4y+8\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4x+8\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y+8\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=4y-8\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=0.5.$ Given that the point $P(0.5,2,4)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=y+2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)+\\frac{1}{x}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=0.5.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(0.5,2,4)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(0.5,2)}.$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(0.5,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(0.5,2)} & =2+2(2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡((0.5)(2))+\\frac{1}{0.5} \\\\  & =2+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+2 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(0.5,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(0.5,2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-4 & =4(y-2) \\\\ z & =4y-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(0.5,2,4)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=0.5 \\\\ z=4y-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/r