ue" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=0.5 \\\\ z=4y-12\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=0.5 \\\\ z=4y-4\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=4x+2\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36441" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=0.5 \\\\ z=4y-4\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=2.$ Given that the point $P(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2,2\\pi )$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{xy}{\\pi }$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2,2\\pi )$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(-\\pi /2,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(-\\pi /2,2)} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})(2)}{\\pi } \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(-\\pi /2,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(-\\pi /2,2)}(x-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\ z-2\\pi  & =-2(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ z & =-2x+\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},2,2\\pi )$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=-2x+\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9f77ab83ff0ba5aac801d22370afc5a675d44ad23b296279e6507db4f0f22b6" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=-2x+\\pi \\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=-2x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=2x-2\\pi \\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=x+2\\pi \\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132590" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=x-\\pi \\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=e.$ Given that the point $P(e,2,3)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{{x}^{2}}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=e.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(e,2,3)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(e,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(e,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(e,2) & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(e,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(e,2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =1(y-2) \\\\ z & =y+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(e,2,3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=e \\\\ z=y+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9f77ab83ff0ba5aac801d22370afc5a675d44ad23b296279e6507db4f0f22b6" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=e \\\\ z=2y-1\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa236e45f6e067050b9e1c6a89a7a69e46a8589fec7b1586f51e8a36847f56" "basis" 1638 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-132589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=e \\\\ z=2y-3\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044096/state.json" "file_sha256" "90aa23